f(x, y, z) & =x y z \\

\overline{\nabla f} & =\hat{i} f_{x}+\hat{j} f_{y}+\hat{k} f_{z} \\

& =\hat{i}(y z)+\hat{j}(x z)+\hat{k}(x y) \\

\overline{\nabla f}_{(0,2,1)} & =\hat{i}(2)+0 \hat{j}+0 \hat{k}

\end{aligned}$$

Directional derivative,

$$\begin{aligned}

D \cdot D & =\overline{\nabla f} \cdot \frac{\bar{a}}{|\bar{a}|} \\

& =(2 \hat{i}+0 \hat{j}+0 \hat{k}) \cdot \frac{(2 \hat{i}+\hat{j}+2 \hat{k})}{\sqrt{2^{2}+1^{2}+2^{2}}}=\frac{4}{\sqrt{9}}=\frac{4}{3}

\end{aligned}$$

Therefore, the correct answer is **B**.

